WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.000
Welcome back.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Have you ever considered that your primary role

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.320
isn't just to manage work, but it's to multiply talent?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.640
We call this the manager multiplier effect.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.500
The idea is very simple.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.660
Your leadership is a catalyst.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.140
Your actions, your coaching, your alignment,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.580
don't just add to your team's output, they multiply it.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.500
When you effectively coach one player,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.620
their increased performance and engagement and alignment

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.620
lifts the entire team and drives measurable business results.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.500
You're not on the sidelines.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.660
You're driving how your direct report

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.660
and your broader team applies M.V.P. in real time.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.380
I saw this with a manager named David.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.720
He invested the time in coaching his player, Kim,

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.980
on her presentation skills.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:55.140
Now, Kim then led a high stakes client pitch

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.820
that her team won.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.900
The winning boosted the team morale,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.700
secured a major contract,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.820
and got the whole team recognized by senior leadership.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.500
David's one coaching investment was multiplied

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.040
into a team win and a business win.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:16.500
Your play is to identify one area

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.860
where your player's growth could have a multiplier effect

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.420
on the team.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.740
Is it their technical skills?

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.940
Maybe their ability to collaborate?

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.640
Note this in your playbook.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:32.100
This becomes a strategic focus for your coaching.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.480
Think about your team's biggest goal for this quarter.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.460
How could you align stakeholders outside of your immediate team

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.040
to align on shared goals and execution?

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.400
Have you translated direction from your senior leaders

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.520
into clear, actionable steps for your team?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.800
How can your player's development in this program

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.000
directly contribute to achieving that goal?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.160
Could this insight to your direct report

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.160
create greater alignment through the 90-day plan?

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.920
Let's be specific.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.200
Use the multiplier effect.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.560
Drill in your playbook to capture your thoughts

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.300
on these questions.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.280
In our next segment, we'll get tactical

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.640
about how to set the stage for this kind of impact

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:18.920
with your player.
